<title>USA: Trade not seen dominating Clinton-Hashimoto talks.</title>
<headline>Trade not seen dominating Clinton-Hashimoto talks.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>White House spokesman Mike McCurry said on Thursday that he did not expect the issue of trade to dominate a meeting between President Bill Clinton and Japanese Prime Minister Ryutaro Hashimoto next week.</p>
<p>Asked if he expected the issue to dominate the session, scheduled for Friday, April 25, McCurry replied: &quot;No, because ... remember we have in place structural agreements to deal with a lot of our trade concerns.&quot;</p>
</text>
